    "search_badge_styles": {
      "_comment": "How each badge in the menu and the chips is drawn, measured from the report's own CSS (docs/design-search.md §7a). Keys: a tag's folded name (a row's id after `tag:`, a token's styleKey) or a speaker code. Colours are display-P3, 0…1. `bg` null means no fill; `border` null means none; a person's `name` null means the badge shows the code alone. `padX`/`padY` are the left and top padding; `padRight`/`padBottom` the other sides (a name half is padded on one side only); `lineHeightPx` null means the CSS left it `normal`.",
      "wire": {
